Meet Clara Serrajordi: Barcelona=E2=80=99s midfield hope filling the void l=
eft by Alexia Putellas | Moving the Goalposts | Football | The Guardian


Meet Clara Serrajordi: Barcelona=E2=80=99s midfield hope filling the void l=
eft by Alexia Putellas


The 18-year-old on being thrown in at the deep end with the first team, pla=
ying with her idols and replacing a legend


=E2=80=98It=E2=80=99s been incredible to grow up here and to be able to get=
 to the first team =E2=80=93 a dream that every girl at the club has.=E2=80=
=99 Clara Serrajordi has won a Champions League and two league titles at Ba=
rcelona. Photograph: Raquel Alvarado/The Guardian


Alex Ibaceta in Barcelona


The next move on the chess board could not have been clearer for Barcelona =
and their coach, Pere Romeu: a new queen has broken into the
Blaugrana
midfield. Clara Serrajordi has made substantial moves already: she made her=
 first-team debut at the age of 17, started ahead of Aitana Bonmat=C3=AD in=
 the 2026 Champions League final and is filling the void left by the depart=
ed Alexia Putellas this season.

Serrajordi is a keen chess player and uses it to disconnect from football a=
nd there are similarities to how she plays. A pure representation of a
La Masia
-educated midfielder, she is always one move ahead, conscious of the space =
around her and fully aware of the importance of each teammate.

Serrajordi was scouted at the age of 11 in 2018 when playing for CE Llerona=
 who were in the same league as Barcelona=E2=80=99s
alev=C3=ADn
team. =E2=80=9CI would play against them and they were so good,=E2=80=9D sh=
e reflects as she sits down with Moving the Goalposts. =E2=80=9CI thought t=
o myself, those girls are going to be my teammates and I didn=E2=80=99t bel=
ieve it at first. I would just repeat to myself: =E2=80=98I=E2=80=99m going=
 to be with the best=E2=80=99.=E2=80=9D


=E2=80=98I thought to myself, those girls are going to be my teammates.=E2=
=80=99 A young Clara Serrajordi playing for CE Llerona against Barcelona. P=
hotograph: Courtesy of Clara Serrajordi


At 18 years old it can be difficult to imagine what lies ahead and even tho=
ugh Barcelona give academy products more chances than almost anywhere else =
in elite football, the statistics are not great. There is no official perce=
ntage but an investigation done by
https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IR8g1=
B4hxqFkYkIbzGOwdxy0fqmE5jJNRlC4Xfki5Jf7-L_B32L_Ae4T4EdxzneCZrTuLakxhDifgmnO=
wfLwfbEhoZtZlS40nraOV5q0OhQUzSOX9J2Q-vCrDDha-vhgMOG0ECjfnPLLVkGLb1pz4keyxD9=
OBpA5-WUm4QkKxEWiMvpGuPUMwLMS3sjFN_l5CEOlrUBOM7B1aSSmeFI8bD4F3yoq0S1CzrIdR1=
daebdNu-m0B96oCi59AcIPuGOOnEpvep6eqGiOZYnO3YQZb5A_5sGyBto65HxEMFMRih3RttmfU=
QQevCEPoPMmUQAxLjZ0D1vDLITj1ixViGxutbAM/4vh/hDkE9cD4RdOmzL2i-bZxCQ/t0/h001.=
NeTTa828Hp-o8YNEPYgZimGq7KvJXny4pTKcae9IiCY
Mundo Deportivo
in 2022 concluded that only 2-5% of the men=E2=80=99s
La Masia
players make it to the first team. The figure may well be the same for the =
women=E2=80=99s side.

=E2=80=9CWhen I first signed I never thought I would achieve everything tha=
t I have,=E2=80=9D says Serrajordi, who has already won a Champions League,=
 two league titles, two Copa de la Reinas and one Supercopa. =E2=80=9CIt=E2=
=80=99s been incredible to grow up here and to be able to get to the first =
team =E2=80=93 a dream that every girl at the club has. When you first arri=
ve at the club, you don=E2=80=99t think you=E2=80=99re going to make it to =
the first team.=E2=80=9D


Serrajordi surges past OL Lyonnes=E2=80=99 Lily Yohannes during Barcelona=
=E2=80=99s triumph in the 2026 Champions League final. Photograph: Yves Her=
man/Reuters


In the 2025-26 season, Serrajordi started 19 of 26 league matches she playe=
d in, totalling a goal and three assists along the way. She sustained an ar=
m fracture at the beginning of this season and was out for a month, but has=
 already totalled 311 minutes on the pitch.

=E2=80=9CI didn=E2=80=99t think that I would make it to the first team unti=
l I started playing for the B team and I would go train with the first team=
 every so often,=E2=80=9D she adds. =E2=80=9CI would say, =E2=80=98wow, I=
=E2=80=99m training with the best, I hope I can make it and play a game wit=
h them.=E2=80=99 And when I started being called up for matchday squads, th=
at=E2=80=99s when I first thought, =E2=80=98I=E2=80=99m here, and can actua=
lly make it=E2=80=99.=E2=80=9D


Serrajordi (centre) as a fan, taking a selfie with Alexia Putellas. Photogr=
aph: Courtesy of Clara Serrajordi


In May of this year Romeu picked Serrajordi to start the Champions League f=
inal against OL Lyonnes in Oslo. Barcelona won 4-0 and Serrajordi won her f=
irst Champions League. You feel it will not be the last. =E2=80=9CI didn=E2=
=80=99t expect [to be a starter], honestly. I found out in the pre-match ta=
lk and when [Romeu] told me, I only thought =E2=80=98OK, we need to go out =
with everything and fight for the most important title of the season.=E2=80=
=99 For me, it was a dream and to have achieved that in my first year; it w=
as special.=E2=80=9D


=E2=80=98All the midfielders that come from the academy have a very similar=
 style of play. We all have the Bar=C3=A7a style.=E2=80=99 Serrajordi has a=
lready totalled 311 minutes on the pitch. Photograph: Raquel Alvarado/The G=
uardian


There are clear similarities between the Llinars del Vall=C3=A8s native and=
 Putellas, physically and footballistically. Serrajordi was taken under the=
 Barcelona captain=E2=80=99s wing and seems like the most natural replaceme=
nt for the midfield legend, who left her childhood club to join London City=
 Lionesses last summer.

=E2=80=9CIn the end, Alexia is an indisputable Bar=C3=A7a player,=E2=80=9D =
says Serrajordi. =E2=80=9CAll the years that she was at the club and everyt=
hing that she=E2=80=99s shown the world, she=E2=80=99s one of a kind, and n=
o one can be like her. But in terms of style of play, we all play very simi=
lar.

=E2=80=9CAll the midfielders that come from the academy have a very similar=
 style of play. We all have the Bar=C3=A7a style and she definitely has it.=
 So, there are some similarities, yes, but I can only hope to one day becom=
e like her, but I still have a lot of things to improve.=E2=80=9D

The balance between youth and experience at Barcelona is a key part of the =
success of the club. With departures and injuries, the
blaugrana
club has been forced to rely on their academy prospects to fill in the big =
gaps on the pitch and in the dressing room.

=E2=80=9CI had always followed the first team and all the players,=E2=80=9D=
 Serrajordi says when asked what it was like to play with her idols. =E2=80=
=9CFrom the first moment they adopted me and all the younger players who ca=
me into the first team. Because of that, we=E2=80=99re able to perform on t=
he pitch the way we do, they give us confidence to play our game.

=E2=80=9CTo be surrounded by the best in the world is easy. A lot of people=
 say, wow, Serra plays really well, but Serra wouldn=E2=80=99t play like th=
is if she wasn=E2=80=99t next to Patri [Guijarro], Aitana, Alexia and all m=
y teammates.=E2=80=9D

